Never Existed", "last_comment_created": 1790435497307, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 16, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "Jane Smith, the now-former CEO of Family First Credit Union in Saginaw, Michigan, is no longer employed by the company after an AI-generated family photograph joking about President Donald Trump\u2019s renaming of Lake Ontario went viral and sparked an online backlash.\u00a0Smith had been preparing for a 10-day family trip to Halifax, Nova Scotia, when her family took a photograph at Detroit Metropolitan Airport. Using ChatGPT, Smith altered the image to make it appear that the family was wearing matching sweatshirts emblazoned with the words \u201cLake America\u201d \u2014 the name Trump ordered the federal government to use for Lake Ontario.The image was shared publicly on Facebook earlier this month with the caption, \u201cLike our sweatshirts? Not sure Canada will. Lol lol.\u201d\u00a0The family never actually wore the sweatshirts. Smith told ABC12 that the photograph was meant as a joke about the renaming rather than a political statement. She said the image was originally posted privately with an indication that it had been AI-generated befo", "large_image": "2goZmcinjIQSEQq1.png", "title": "CEO Out Of A Job Over \u2018Lake America\u2019 Sweatshirts That Never Existed"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVQtWnKa", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 583, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8855650, "raw_content": "", "author": "Eruditio", "created": 1790353881995, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Induceddrag", "is_video": fals